      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STAR DECORUM (9) ran a better race and finished fourth last time out over 1900m at Quorn. Is mixing her form but is a track and trip winner that can win again here if she brings her A-game. CARASHAN CHLOE (6) has struggled to threaten of late despite the market support but does boast peaks that are superior. Ran well over this track and trip earlier in the prep when sent out fav on June 7. Has built a decent association with Hutchinson. UNISPHERE (7) got the prize two runs ago at Balaklava in testing conditions but was less effective here last time when only managing fourth. Has been freshened with 5 weeks between runs and gets a great opportunity to get things straight back on track.  LETTEMGO (4) has been in the placings at his last two appearances, finishing third over 1900m at Quorn most recently. Among the chances. CRACKEN GOOD TIME (5) doesn't win out of turn but draws well here and looks best of the rest on his best form.",
